//? Title: Forward Euler: Actual Tangents, Error and Stability Limits
//? Subtitle: Checked vector ODE integration with native C++ trajectories, derivative histories and exact work counts
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given an initial state and its rate of change, forward Euler advances
along the current derivative once per fixed step. We begin with two
hand-checkable decay steps, retain the original coarse trajectory and
error-refinement experiment, and distinguish first-order accuracy from
stability. The same core execution returns actual states, derivatives
and work counts. Scalar decay, an oscillator, time-dependent forcing
and finite numerical boundaries expose what this simple method can and
cannot establish. Successful execution supplies no adaptive error bound.
)

\toc

> Two actual tangent steps

For y'=-y with y(0)=1 and h=1/2, the first derivative is -1, giving
y[1]=1+(1/2)(-1)=1/2. At this approximate state, the next derivative is
-1/2, giving y[2]=1/2+(1/2)(-1/2)=1/4. The exact value at t=1 is
exp(-1), about 0.367879. The second step uses the derivative of the
ODE field at the approximate state, not a tangent to the exact curve
at that time. Both derivatives below come from the actual solver call.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euler_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::euler_method_trace([](double,const std::vector<double>& y){return std::vector<double>{-y[0]};},{1},0,1,2);
  const auto& s=t.outcome.solution;
  std::print("Tiny Euler: h {}; samples {}; derivative calls {}; scalar updates {}; entries {}; final y {}; exact {:.12f}.\n\n",t.outcome.step_size,s.t.size(),t.outcome.work.rhs_calls,t.outcome.work.scalar_updates,t.captured_entries,s.y.back()[0],std::exp(-1.));
  std::print("| actual step | time before | state before | returned derivative | time after | state after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(430,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramStroke green;green.color={22,163,74};green.width=3;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke blue;blue.color={37,99,235};blue.width=4;std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> exact;
  for(int i=0;i<=100;++i){const double x=i/100.;exact.push_back({x,std::exp(-x)});}d.path(exact,green);
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.derivatives.size();++i){std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,s.t[i],s.y[i][0],t.derivatives[i][0],s.t[i+1],s.y[i+1][0]);d.path({{s.t[i],s.y[i][0]},{s.t[i+1],s.y[i+1][0]}},blue);}
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<s.t.size();++i)d.ellipse({s.t[i],s.y[i][0]},.015,.015,{37,99,235});
  d.path({{0,0},{1.1,0}}).path({{0,0},{0,1.15}}).text({-.1,1},"1",20).text({.5,-.1},"t=0.5",20).text({1,-.1},"t=1",20)
   .label({.25,.82},"slope -1",20).label({.8,.22},"slope -0.5",20).text({.5,1.38},"Actual Euler steps and exact decay",26)
   .text({.5,-.32},"Blue Euler states; green exp(-t)",22).save_svg("build/euler_tiny.svg");
}
