> Stability is different from accuracy

On the scalar test equation y'=lambda y, Euler multiplies the state
by R(z)=1+z, with z=h lambda. Absolute stability means |1+z|<=1,
the closed disk centered at -1 with radius one in the complex plane.
Strict decay of the numerical homogeneous solution requires |1+z|<1.
For real decay y'=-a y with a>0 and positive h, put q=h a. Then
0<q<2 gives decay; 0<q<1 stays positive, 1<q<2 alternates sign,
q=2 alternates without damping, and q>2 grows. q=1 reaches zero
in one step. Stability alone supplies no desired accuracy tolerance.

The table evaluates actual integrations and the existing native
stability_function API. The disk is a mathematical concept diagram;
its marked real-axis points correspond to the measured q values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euler_stability.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::print("| q=h*a | R(-q) | absolute amplification | actual y after 8 | closed discrete y after 8 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(240,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramStroke border;border.color={37,99,235};border.width=3;
  d.ellipse({-1,0},1,1,{219,234,254},border).path({{-2.9,0},{.45,0}}).path({{0,-1.3},{0,1.3}});
  for(double q:{.5,1.,1.5,2.,2.5}){const auto r=dm::algorithms::euler_method_work([q](double,const std::vector<double>& y){return std::vector<double>{-2*q*y[0]};},{1},0,4,8);const auto z=dm::algorithms::stability_function(dm::algorithms::OdeMethod::ForwardEuler,{-q,0});std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",q,z.real(),std::abs(z),r.solution.y.back()[0],std::pow(z.real(),8));d.ellipse({-q,0},.025,.025,q<2?dm::graphics::RGB{37,99,235}:dm::graphics::RGB{220,38,38}).text({-q,q==1||q==2?.2:-.2},std::format("z=-{}",q),19);}
  d.text({-1,.55},"|1+z| <= 1",26).text({-.05,1.5},"Im z",22).text({.5,-.2},"Re z",22).text({-1.2,1.9},"Forward Euler absolute stability disk",26).text({-1.2,-1.7},"Boundary q=2 is neutral; q>2 grows",22).save_svg("build/euler_stability.svg");
}
