> Oscillations expose the imaginary-axis limitation

For the harmonic oscillator x'=v, v'=-x, exact energy
E=(x^2+v^2)/2 is constant. Forward Euler instead maps
(x,v) to (x+h v,v-h x), so

\[
x_{n+1}^2+v_{n+1}^2=(1+h^2)(x_n^2+v_n^2),\qquad
E_n/E_0=(1+h^2)^n.
\]

Every nonzero real h therefore pumps energy into this oscillator.
Its eigenvalues are imaginary, and |1+i h|>1 places them outside the
Euler stability disk. Reducing h reduces the growth over a fixed
finite interval, but does not turn the method into an energy-preserving
integrator. The following plot uses the actual two-component trace;
the energy formula is an independent closed discrete check.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euler_oscillator.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto t=dm::algorithms::euler_method_trace([](double,const std::vector<double>& y){return std::vector<double>{y[1],-y[0]};},{1,0},0,20,2000);const auto& s=t.outcome.solution;const double h=t.outcome.step_size;
  std::vector<double> x,v,exact_x,exact_v,energy,theory;double maxerror=0;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<s.t.size();++i){const auto& y=s.y[i];x.push_back(y[0]);v.push_back(y[1]);exact_x.push_back(std::cos(s.t[i]));exact_v.push_back(-std::sin(s.t[i]));energy.push_back(std::log(y[0]*y[0]+y[1]*y[1]));theory.push_back(i*std::log1p(h*h));maxerror=std::max(maxerror,std::abs(energy.back()-theory.back()));}
  std::print("Oscillator: h {}; actual calls {}; scalar updates {}; final x {:.12g}; final v {:.12g}.\n",h,t.outcome.work.rhs_calls,t.outcome.work.scalar_updates,x.back(),v.back());
  std::print("Energy ratio measured {:.12f}; discrete formula {:.12f}; max log-ratio error {:.3g}.\n",std::exp(energy.back()),std::exp(theory.back()),maxerror);
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(exact_x,exact_v,"exact",{22,163,74}).line(x,v,"Euler",{37,99,235}).title("Actual Euler orbit spirals outward").x_label("Position x").y_label("Velocity v");
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(s.t,theory,"n*log(1+h*h)",{220,38,38}).line(s.t,energy,"actual energy",{37,99,235}).title("Energy grows at every nonzero step").x_label("Time t").y_label("Natural log(E / initial E)");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,520).title("First-order accuracy does not imply long-time energy conservation").fit_panels().save_svg("build/euler_oscillator.svg");
}
